type(scope): subject of at most 72 characters, imperative

Why the change exists, then what it does. Wrap at 72. One blank line
above this paragraph and one above the trailer block.

# Agents: do not rely on this template. Write the message to a file
# without '#' lines (git keeps them under -F), commit with
# `git commit -F <file>`, then add the trailers from the file:
#   git interpret-trailers --in-place --if-exists addIfDifferent \
#     --trailer "$(cat .git-trailers)" <file>
# and commit afterwards. The trailer block is the last paragraph;
# a stray heredoc tail breaks its parsing (8ab88e2).
